  "description": "ILGPU/CUDA acceleration for the AlgFormer package's HoloFormer model: GpuHoloTrainer runs batched GPU forward/backward training (CPU Adam by default, with an opt-in fused on-GPU Adam step) and GPU inference (Logits, StackIterLogits). GpuDevice auto-detects a CUDA device at startup and otherwise runs the SAME kernels on ILGPU's own CPU accelerator, so one build works with or without a CUDA card; genuinely over-length windows still run on the CPU HoloFormer directly. Every kernel is gradchecked against the CPU HoloFormer as its correctness oracle (float-close fp32, not bit-identical). Also ships an opt-in, default-OFF \"ADAM & EVE\" per-layer directional gradient gate layered on the fused on-GPU Adam step, live in production training (not an unused experiment) since 2026-09-24, plus preference (DPO) training on the GPU: per-sequence log-probabilities (SequenceLogProb) and a signed-weight all-positions training step (TrainBatchAllPosWeighted), at the same weight-tied depth the trainer trains at, with a frozen reference model (NewReference); exact bit-identical GPU page transforms for Phasor's Pleroma key band (PleromaPageTransform: Forward, Inverse, Dft over a 61-bit or sub-40-bit prime field, with an ILGPU CPU and a managed backend) and the Pleroma Cascade Newton pass (PleromaNewtonGpu); and a deprecated non-holo GpuModel/GpuTrainer twin for the older softmax-attention AlgFormer core. Add this package only if you want GPU acceleration; the core AlgFormer package stays dependency-free and AOT/trim-safe without it.",
